# Code Quality

## File Size

❌ BAD - 300+ line file doing everything:
// AuthScreen.tsx - 350 lines
// validation, API calls, UI, animations, state all in one file

✅ GOOD - split into focused files:
// AuthScreen.tsx - 80 lines (UI only)
// useAuthFlow.ts - 40 lines (logic)
// authValidation.ts - 30 lines (validation)

Max 150 lines/file. Max 50 lines/function.

## Single Responsibility

❌ BAD - component doing too much:
function AuthScreen() {
  // validation logic here
  // API call here
  // animation logic here
  // 15 useState calls
  // render 200 lines of JSX
}

✅ GOOD - one purpose per file:
function AuthScreen() {
  const { signIn, error } = useAuthFlow();
  return <AuthForm onSubmit={signIn} error={error} />;
}

## Naming

❌ BAD:
data.ts, utils.ts, helpers.ts, stuff.tsx, Component1.tsx

✅ GOOD:
userValidation.ts, formatDate.ts, AuthButton.tsx, useAuthFlow.ts
